## Physics Behind
Here we rely on the Verlet integration method, which operates only in coordinate space (no velocities or accelerations need to be stored):

$$
x_{i+1} = 2x_i - x_{i-1} + a_i\, \delta t^2
$$

In our case, we have $a_i = 0$, and only boundary conditions are applied afterward, i.e., this part:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
    balls1 = Map[Function[p, 
      If[Norm[p] > 1,
        HapticFeedback[]; 
        Normalize[p] 0.99
      ,
        p
      ]
    ], (2 balls2 - balls3)];

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
To simulate the "bounce" and loss of energy, we force the balls to stay within the boundaries by applying `Normalize` and multiplying by a slightly smaller number.

